# SPA fallback. App.tsx uses BrowserRouter, so /agents/:agentId and /docs are
# client-side routes with no file behind them. Without this rule Netlify
# resolves the path on the server first and returns its own 404 before React
# ever loads — every deep link and every refresh on a sub-route breaks, while
# clicking through from / works fine. That asymmetry is why it survives casual
# testing.
#
# Must stay last: _redirects is evaluated top-down and this matches everything.
